-- Two records in ONE module, one of whose SOURCE names already carries this module's
-- own mangle prefix.  That is the shape that makes an owner-qualification applied twice
-- collide: `Cfg` qualifies to `Mm__Cfg`, and a second application of the same
-- qualification to the sibling's already-prefixed `Mm__Cfg` leaves it unchanged, so the
-- two records land on ONE emitted head and the emitter picks one layout for both.
--
-- ⚠️ THE MODULE ID MUST START WITH AN UPPER-CASE LETTER, and that is load-bearing:
-- constructors are upper-case, so `lib.sub`'s prefix (`lib_sub__`) is unspellable as a
-- record name and only a module id like `Mm` can be written into one.  Renaming this
-- file silently stops the cell testing anything.
--
-- The field ORDERS are deliberately opposite, so a wrong head is a wrong VALUE rather
-- than merely a wrong name: read through `Cfg`'s layout, `mkB.a` and `mkB.b` swap.
public export data Cfg = { a : Int, b : Int }

public export data Mm__Cfg = { b : Int, a : Int }

export mkA : Cfg
mkA = Cfg { a = 11, b = 22 }

export mkB : Mm__Cfg
mkB = Mm__Cfg { b = 33, a = 44 }
